---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Reveal from "../components/Reveal.astro";
import "../styles/base.css";
import "../styles/pages/terms.css";
---

<Base title={"Terms · Y2O"} description={"The ground rules for using Y2O, in plain language."}>
<header class="hero" style="padding-bottom: 60px">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="tag rv">Terms</span>
    <h1 class="rv d1">The ground rules <em>for using Y2O</em></h1>
    <p class="sub rv d2">Plain language. No surprises.</p>
  </div>
</header>
<section class="sec" style="padding-top: 20px">
  <div class="wrap legal">
    <div class="draft">
      <svg
        width="22"
        height="22"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="2"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
      >
        <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10Z" /></svg
      >A plain-language summary while our full policy is reviewed by legal
      counsel.
    </div>
    <div class="short">
      <h3>The short version</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <svg
            width="20"
            height="20"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5" /></svg
          >Students own their records
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg
            width="20"
            height="20"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5" /></svg
          >Confirmations are made in good faith
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg
            width="20"
            height="20"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5" /></svg
          >Y2O is not a transcript or admissions decision
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg
            width="20"
            height="20"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5" /></svg
          >Organizations own the opportunities they post
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <h2>What Y2O is</h2>
    <p>
      A record of what students do beyond grades, confirmed by the people
      who saw the work, plus a feed of opportunities from organizations.
    </p>
    <h2>What Y2O is not</h2>
    <p>
      Not a transcript or official school record. Not an admissions decision
      tool. Not a guarantee of any job, scholarship, or placement. The
      research we cite is not an endorsement by those organizations.
    </p>
    <h2>Student records</h2>
    <p>
      Students own their records and are responsible for logging activities
      honestly.
    </p>
    <h2>Confirmations</h2>
    <p>
      When a supervisor or organization confirms an activity, they confirm
      it happened as described, to the best of their knowledge.
    </p>
    <h2>Opportunities</h2>
    <p>
      Opportunities are offered by the organizations that post them. Y2O is
      not a party to any role, program, or award.
    </p>
    <h2>Institutional access</h2>
    <p>
      Partner institutions receive anonymised data under a separate
      agreement. Named records are shared only by the student.
    </p>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We'll email account holders before any important change to these
      terms.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:info@youth2opportunities.ca"
        >info@youth2opportunities.ca</a
      >
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
  <Reveal slot="scripts" />
</Base>
